# Project specific -- run outputs, for when a batch is pointed at the repo root.
#
# Named rules, not blanket *.xml / *.md: tests/fixtures/ is full of committed
# XML and the docs are Markdown, so a blanket rule would hide the fixtures this
# suite is built on.
#
# This file is the source for BOTH repos. fetchpdf_public/.gitignore is written
# by tools/make_public.py and is overwritten on every sync, so edit it here.
*.pdf
pdfs/
papers/
downloaded_papers/
test_downloads/
missing_pdfs.html
failed_dois.csv
source_tracking.csv
source_counts.json
provenance.json
references.json
references.md
body.md
*_abstract.md
*_linked_artifacts.json

# Playwright
.playwright/
playwright-state.json

# Institutional access (--cookies / --ebsco). A cookie export is a live
# credential for every site the browser was signed into, and the Chrome
# profile the Playwright driver keeps is the same thing in directory form.
cookies.txt
*cookies*.json
storage_state*.json
.fetchpdf-chrome-profile/

# One-off corpus-audit artifacts. Written by ad-hoc repair runs, not part of the
# package; they name specific DOIs on a specific day and go stale immediately.
/inbox_redownload*.csv
/inbox_redownload*.txt
/OVERNIGHT_STATUS.md
